prompt-creator
------------------------

A /prompt command for OpenCode and FuckCode.

It reads the project, asks up to five clarifying questions, and
saves a ready task prompt to prompts/<date>-<slug>.md that any
AI agent can read and execute.

The command itself is prompt.md.


Install
------------------------

OpenCode or FuckCode must be installed and available in PATH

Linux and macOS:

curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NoNFake/prompt-creator/main/install.sh | bash


From a clone:

git clone https://github.com/NoNFake/prompt-creator.git
cd prompt-creator
./install.sh


The installer detects opencode and fuckcode in PATH and installs
prompt.md as /prompt for each one it finds

The command is copied to:

~/.config/opencode/commands/prompt.md
~/.config/fuckcode/commands/prompt.md

If an existing file differs, it is saved as prompt.md.bak.<date>
before being replaced

Usage
------------------------

/prompt add CSV export for the report

The agent inspects the code, asks up to five questions, then writes
the task prompt. To execute it later:

Read prompts/<file>.md and do it


Inside this repository
------------------------

The command is already active for both tools through symlinks:

.fuckcode/commands/prompt.md -> ../../prompt.md
.opencode/commands/prompt.md -> ../../prompt.md
